{"v":1,"built_at":"2026-10-30T20:47:03.385Z","core":{"appSha":"de48ef3fe09f","builtAt":"2026-10-29T23:27:21.055Z","schemaV":1},"key":"us/119-s-195","model":{"found":true,"billKey":"us/119-s-195","polity":"us","eyebrow":"United States","reference":"S. 195","title":"American Music Tourism Act of 2025","titleExpandable":false,"meta":"Commerce, Science, and Transportation Committee · Sen. Marsha Blackburn (R-TN)","summary":{"lead":"Official summary (Congressional Research Service, Introduced in Senate): ","blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"American Music Tourism Act of 2025","gap":"none"},{"kind":"para","text":"This bill directs the National Travel and Tourism Office (NTTO) of the Department of Commerce to promote tourism to music-related and sports attractions.","gap":"para"},{"kind":"para","text":"The bill requires NTTO to promote domestic and international travel and tourism to U.S. music festivals, concert venues, and other music-related attractions and locations. The bill also expands NTTO's current mandate to facilitate sports and recreation events and activities to include the promotion of international travel and tourism to such activities in the United States.","gap":"para"},{"kind":"para","text":"NTTO must report its activities and findings to Congress within one year after the bill's enactment and, thereafter, every two years.","gap":"para"}]},"pathLabel":"The legislative path","latest":{"labelText":"Signed by Pres. Trump","glyph":{"icon":"scroll","badge":true},"date":"9 October 2026"},"asOf":{"lead":"Record as of ","date":"9 October 2026","note":"the most recent action in the official record. Status can lag; each step below carries its own date."},"groups":[{"spine":{"key":"rec-S. 195-17","kind":"record","spine":true,"date":"9 October 2026","labelText":"Signed by Pres. Trump","glyph":{"icon":"scroll","badge":true},"postId":"us-20261013-20d81fe9","postHref":"/p/us-20261013-20d81fe9","whatsNext":{"lead":"What's next: ","text":"Takes effect (on enactment unless t